it's been 20 years since the beginning  of halo a series that would change the  way we look at console shooters forever  and still being able to play them all to  this day makes it even easier to revisit  our favorites a lot has evolved over the  past two decades for the franchise and  with halo infinite right around the  corner we thought it would be a great  time to take a look at the evolution of  some of our favorite halo weapons  starting with the magnum leave a like  subscribe and let's get to it  in my opinion while the magnum in combat  evolved is the greatest one on the list  today it's almost so good that it left  shoes simply too big to fill so we'll  consider it in a league of its own the  ce magnum is an absolute powerhouse it  takes only three shots to kill from just  about any range and being able to scope  in makes it that much easier to mow down  your enemies in theory with a clip size  of 12 you could wipe a whole squad  without even having to reload if the  star is aligned this was also long  before bloom was something the devs had  to consider for pistols making it even  more dangerous as if all of that wasn't  good enough it can be easy to forget  that we also start with all of the ammo  we could possibly need with 60 bullets  on hand every single time you spawn  needless to say this magnum is one of  the best guns in the series and can make  talking about the next ones a little bit  painful  [Music]  halo 2 is my personal favorite halo and  the one i think the most hours into but  i don't think much of that time was  spent using pistols and it's pretty  obvious why with the addition of dual  welding the power of the magnum was  drastically reduced the fire rate for  the pistol is faster than what it was in  ce but it takes a massive number of 13  shots to get the kill if that sounds  like a lot well it is because the clip  size is still only 12 bullets and you  only spawn with 36 bullets in the pocket  this time around dual wielding with an  energy weapon makes the pistol much more  viable but in the bigger picture of halo  2 we were often opting for a shiny new  battle rifle instead as things like the  double shot became second nature for  some players the pistol served its  purpose by simply being the secondary  weapon to allow a flurry of non-stop vr  bullets and preventing your gun from  jamming to add insult to injury the  scope was also removed from magnum  making it even more difficult to use in  a pinch  halo 3's magnum got a few buffs in  comparison to halo 2 although the bar  was admittedly very low it now takes 5  shots to kill but the fire rate is  slower than the halo 2 magnum and the  clip size is reduced to 8. this makes  the magnum better in finishing off weak  opponents if you could overcome the slow  weapon swapping but still not the type  of weapon you would use as a primary  especially since our spawning ammo  capacity is once again reduced this time  being 32 rounds although this version of  the magnum is a major improvement from  two there is still no ability to scope  which is likely a byproduct of dual  building as halo 2 and 3 were the only  games to allow dual welding with magnums  and also the only two to remove the  scopes from the gun however the accuracy  of the magnum without a scope at a  distance is still surprisingly  consistent ultimately the magnum in pvp  was still in a place where it was being  passed up in favor of the more popular  and practical  rifles when it comes to halo reach it  might be one of my least favorite of the  series in pvp because i personally  wasn't prepared for all of the new  abilities but with that aside this  version of the magnum marked the road to  recovery it's the first magnum since  combat evolved to bring back the scope  and also the first one in the series to  add bloom the fire rate has been bumped  up and we're returning with a 5 shot  kill in an 8 round clip just like halo  3. however this time we're starting with  an abysmal 24 shots of magnum ammo  adding quite a sense of urgency to  scavenging scopeless magnums from halo 2  and 3 were already a thing of the past  at this point but the accuracy of the  reach version of the gun was much less  consistent at a distance even with the  scope taking into consideration that  halo reach also had a lot of new  elements for players to adapt to such as  better long range marksman rifles armor  lock and other abilities it's easy to  overlook the magnum and its improvements  however this magnum can go toe-to-toe  with the other rifles in the game and at  least you still feel capable of putting  down team shots from long range instead  of watching helplessly from a distance  and hoping your hail mary grenade  doesn't friendly fire  halo 4's magnum is almost a pleasant  surprise it takes six quick shots to  kill and the fire rate has remained  somewhat consistent with its previous  version in reach halo 4's magnum is  definitely viable but i often find  myself running out of ammo right in the  middle of a fight the clip size is the  same as halo 3 and reach with 8 shots at  your disposal but we're once again  spawning with 24 rounds in total which  makes it absolutely crucial to scavenge  ammo from your enemies but that's  uniquely difficult in halo 4 since  players can choose their own loadout  this means there isn't as much of a  guarantee to run into magnum ammo when  you get a kill ultimately another big  big big big downfall for the magnum in  halo 4 was the removal of the d scope  mechanic making it even more difficult  to take on other rifles especially at a  range  halo 5 is one of my favorite games in  the series and the magnum made a big  return as a viable primary weapon and a  deadly threat it takes five shots to  kill and this time around we're blessed  with a 12 round clip our starting ammo  capacity is up to 36 but with its  viability finding ammo off of your  enemies is much more common the scope  and bloom return but the bloom doesn't  impact the magnum's accuracy at a range  nearly as much as it did in halo reach  the d-scope making a return also makes a  big difference in taking on fights  against other rifles and adds even more  practicality to the gun with the  additional core movement options such as  the thrusts you can now outmaneuver your  opponents in different ways that make  the magnum even more satisfactory when  you get those clean reversals  we're tossing the halo infinite magnum  on this list after getting our hands on  the technical preview but it's worth  noting that the build we played on was a  few months old and not exactly what  we'll be seeing at launch however the  magnum in infinite so far is looking  like a formidable weapon the fire rate  fills close to that of the halo 2 magnum  and takes seven quick shots to kill that  sounds like a lot considering it's the  second most bullets needed behind halo 2  but there's something about the fire  rate and the snappy reload time that  makes it feel lightning fast it  currently sits with a 12 round clip size  and a starting ammo capacity of 48 which  is the second most since ce the bloom on  infinite's gun is actually what makes  the biggest difference up close a rapid  fire seven shot perfect kill feels  nearly impossible to miss so the bloom  doesn't get in the way too much but  apply that same strategy at a range and  you're shooting blanks there will be a  bit of mastery with this iteration but  definitely one of the strongest versions  so far even up against other rifles as  the scope returns and the d scope  mechanic is in full effect  we've seen the magnum in so many ways  shapes and forms but which magnum in the  series is your favorite let us know in  the comments and if you enjoyed this  video then be sure you subscribe for  more we'll be covering all things halo  here on gamespot so stay with us to stay  up to date thanks for watching and we'll  see you next time peace  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

